            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "NG+ is the natural grade, intended for the narrower joints found on standard concrete pavers. SG+ is the stone grade, formulated for the wider, irregular joints of natural flagstone. Using the narrow-joint product in a wide gap is the most common way to make a premium sand fail, so measure before ordering.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does DOMINATOR leave haze on pavers?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Far less than budget sands, which is one of the strongest reasons to pay for it. It is not haze-proof, though — if the paver faces are not swept and blown clean before watering, any polymeric sand will leave a film. The premium buys tolerance, not immunity.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How does DOMINATOR compare to Gator Maxx?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Both are premium sands and both outperform the big-box bags clearly. Gator Maxx has a slight edge on very wide joints and is more widely stocked; DOMINATOR has a broader colour range and holds its colour better over several seasons. On a standard patio the difference between them is small compared with the difference between either and a budget bag.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
