            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For standard narrow joints on concrete pavers, roughly one 50 lb bag per 50 to 100 square feet. Wide joints, thick pavers or irregular flagstone can cut that to 20 to 30 square feet per bag. Order one bag more than the calculation suggests so the whole area cures on the same day.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does DOMINATOR crack?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Correctly installed joints stay flexible enough to handle normal seasonal movement without cracking. Cracking almost always traces to under-filled joints, a base that is moving, or the wrong grade for the joint width — a narrow-joint product bridging a wide gap has nothing to hold onto and splits.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is DOMINATOR worth the extra money?",
