          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">DOMINATOR earns its premium</strong> in the two places that decide how a paved surface looks years later: how little haze it leaves on the paver faces, and how well the joint colour holds. On a patio you will look at every day, that is a sensible place to spend an extra thirty or forty dollars a bag.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Match the grade to your joint width, order it several days before you need it, and remember that no bag rescues a rushed installation. Dry surface, joints filled to depth, faces blown clean, watered exactly as directed — do that, and this is as good as jointing sand gets for a homeowner.
